# Generated by the umbrella release.sh — do not hand-edit except to test an unreleased upstream
# locally (any git ref works: a tag, a branch, a SHA). The next release overwrites it.
#
# The upstream refs this botmaker-dashboard release is built against.
# Consumer: the `package` job of .github/workflows/ci.yml. It checks these four repos out at
# these refs and `mvn install`s them at 0.0.0-SNAPSHOT, so the release build resolves them from
# source and never touches JitPack at all. The file is also baked into the packaged app, which
# compares CLI_TAG against the checkout's botmaker-cli at start-up.
#
# Why a file rather than a version in the pom, and why an exact ref rather than the newest tag: the
# botmaker umbrella's CLAUDE.md, section "Every released module records its upstream refs in a .deps.env".

SHARED_TAG=v0.0.27
STUDIO_API_TAG=v0.1.7
